---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="About" description="Why a new AI safety group at Northeastern, and what is specific to Northeastern.">
  <section class="band">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h1>About</h1>

      <p>
        AI systems are becoming more capable and dangerous at a rate faster than we can control
        them. Models are now able to
        <a href="https://openai.com/index/hugging-face-incident-and-the-road-ahead/">hack into other companies</a>,
        <a href="https://www.anthropic.com/research/agentic-misalignment">blackmail users</a>,
        <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2505.23836">know when they’re being evaluated</a>, and
        even be
        <a href="https://www.anthropic.com/news/disrupting-AI-espionage">used en masse for cyber espionage</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        We want to give Northeastern students the tools and knowledge they need to help align and
        govern AI systems.
      </p>

      <div class="row">
        <h2>Why Northeastern?</h2>
        <div>
        <p>
          Boston is home to one of the most active AI safety communities in the world. Student
          groups at Harvard, MIT and BU have built serious programs, and organizations such as the
          Cambridge Boston Alignment Initiative support research across the region. Few places
          offer students closer proximity to the field.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Northeastern is no stranger to AI safety research.</strong> Professor David Bau’s
          lab in Khoury College is among the leading groups in mechanistic interpretability, the
          study of how neural networks work internally. It also leads the
          <a href="https://ndif.us">National Deep Inference Fabric (NDIF)</a>, an NSF-funded
          project that lets researchers across the country study the inner workings of AI models.
        </p>
        <p>
          We want to take advantage of Northeastern’s incredibly diverse programs to bring
          together students from every college to help align AI systems.
        </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="row">
        <h2>What we do</h2>
        <div>
        <ul>
          <li>A weekly reading group covering everything from fundamentals to current research</li>
          <li>Guest talks from researchers across the Boston area and beyond</li>
          <li>Support and compute for research projects</li>
          <li>Connection to the AI safety community</li>
        </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
